  The window ends (late@0 = early@L = KV@0 = the clean S run; early@0 = late@L = none = the clean B run) and their complementarity (early on [0, l) and late on [l, L) together = KV@0) are FP32-tested (tests/test_stage9_stories.py, test_stage9_passages.py); no GPU check.
  BF16 floor: the none row (edits: self) against the clean B run of the same item in another batch shape (stories: clean_B of the capture pass; passages: clean_B of the capture batch; edits: the CAA batch's self row, unclamped): the mean absolute difference of E (passages: of the decision log-probabilities lp) and the share of items whose argmax answer differs (E-argmax; passages: the decision-token argmax; edits also the generated answers). In-batch determinism: none against none2 (edits: self against self2), the same ids and tables in one forward (0 expected, also in BF16). LETTER: the letter answers whose text names another candidate word ("A drawer" read as option A), a sensitivity count; the answer stays SPEC 9.2's.
